    "preamble": "Nand Lal Gupta vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Food ... on 23 October, 2024 Author: Alok Mathur Bench: Alok Mathur High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:71261 Court No. - 6 Case :- Writ - A No. - 9757 of 2024 Petitioner :- Nand Lal Gupta Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Food Safety Durg Administration Deptt. Gov Counsel for Petitioner :- Akhilesh Kumar Mishra Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C. Hon'ble Alok Mathur,J. Nand Lal Gupta vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Food ... on 23 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/197193422/ 1 3.",
    "facts": "The disciplinary proceedings were concluded on 29.06.2012 wherein the petitioner was reinstated in service and the petitioner was exonerated from all the charges.",
    "arguments": "2. It has been submitted by learned counsel for petitioner that the petitioner is working on the post of Food Safety Officer in the Department of Food Safety and Drug Administration when disciplinary proceedings were initiated against him in 2010 and the petitioner was placed under suspension. It has been submitted by learned counsel for the petitioner that the respondents have not passed any order with regard to payment of full salary to the petitioner during the period he was under suspension, accordingly has made a prayer for a direction to the respondents to pay the amount due to him for the period he has spent as suspension. 4."
  },
